## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end design for long-form audio with multi-chapter outputs, requiring integration of Transcribe, SageMaker, OpenSearch, and DynamoDB, plus governance, privacy, and cross-account considerations.

## Key Concepts

- AWS Transcribe: language auto-detect, diarization
- Time-based chunking of transcripts
- SageMaker endpoint for per-chapter summaries
- OpenSearch and DynamoDB indexing for chapter search
- S3 storage with timestamped prefixes and encryption
- Data lineage with Glue and auditing/tracking
- Cross-account access, IAM least-privilege, DLQ, cost controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: chunk transcript, call SageMaker per chapter, write outputs
async function processChapteredTranscript(transcript) {
  const chapters = chunkByTime(transcript);
  for (const c of chapters) {
    const summary = await sageMaker.summarize(c.text);
    await s3.put(`episode/${transcript.episodeId}/${c.start}-${c.end}.txt`, c.text);
    await s3.put(`episode/${transcript.episodeId}/${c.start}-${c.end}.summary.txt`, summary);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How do you ensure idempotent re-processing for re-uploaded files?
- What operational metrics and alerts would you set for cost and quality drift?
